<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids down, sales mixed.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids down, sales mixed.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat cash bids dropped on Wednesday in line with lower CBOT, KCBT and MGE futures, dealers said.</p>
<p>MGE December wheat lost 8-3/4 cents at $4.13-1/2 a bushel.</p>
<p>But farm sales were sporadic with virtually nothing from the country in parts of Minnesota and a pickup of farmer interest in Washington state.</p>
<p>&quot;Farmers are still hanging on pretty tight,&quot; one Minneapolis dealer said. &quot;If we can offer farmers $4.00-$4.25 a bushel spring wheat, then they might give some up.&quot;</p>
<p>In Washington state, one dealer said movement was beginning to pick up as farmers were concerned about lower futures prices.  </p>
